last_model.pt
best_model.pt.corrupted
results.tsv.corrupted

# One-shot architecture-diagnostic sentinels (local-only).
.auxiliary_diagnostic_done
.auxiliary_diagnostic_0p2_done
smoke_test_config.json
hard_smoke_test_config.json
reports/nnunetv2_baseline_*/
reports/lasagna_fiber_candidates/
scripts/curated_data/
# Generated by the GP-winner and LeJEPA launchers (with this machine's paths) and
# by the proofreader launcher (with the paths it is given), on every run.
scripts/_gp_winner_runner.py
scripts/_finetune_lejepa_runner.py
/proofreader_config.json

# Scratch / debug probes and their outputs (transient, not for the repo)
/debug_*.py
/debug_*.png
/models/
/outputs/
# Dated local archive of retired root files (workspace hygiene, kept off the repo)
/archive/

# Accidental local interpreter symlinks
/python
/python3

# Model Checkpoints
checkpoints/
autoresearch.out

# Loop process state. Ownership is an fcntl lock on the lock file's inode, so a
# tracked lock let `git checkout -- .` / `git stash` / `git restore .` replace the
# file under a running loop and admit a second one (see
# docs/DESIGN_ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW_2026-10-12_CROSS_CUTTING.md).
autoresearch.lock
.current_day_shift_log
# The incumbent held across a training run, and the model of a run that replaced
# it and then failed (run_autoresearch_loop.settle_incumbent).
.best_model.pt.held
best_model.pt.failed-run-*
# Temporaries of the atomic writers (save_checkpoint_atomic, the loop's JSON
# state), left only if a process is killed (SIGKILL) mid-write.
.*.tmp

# Discord DRAFTS stay local-only. What was actually POSTED is tracked: a file that calls
# itself "the public artifact of record" is not a record if it only exists on one machine.
# Negations must come after the pattern they exempt.
docs/DISCORD_*.md
DISCORD_*.md
!docs/DISCORD_POSTED_*.md
!DISCORD_POSTED_*.md

# Community-signal logs may include third-party handles + message text
# from Discord / GitHub; keep local-only to avoid re-publishing others'
# content without consent.
reports/community_signal_*.md
# Generated daily-report PDFs. Regenerated with an embedded timestamp, so they show up
# dirty and produce a meaningless commit every time the generator runs (the 2026-08-14
# file's entire diff was 2 bytes of timestamp). Untracked 2026-08-14; the files stay on
# disk and remain in git history if an old one is ever needed.
reports/Vesuvius_Research_Report_*.pdf
community_signal_*.md

# Skeleton-distance metric writes histogram PNGs to cwd every validation
# cycle (one per sample plus an aggregate). They get overwritten on each
# run and were polluting commits. Local-only diagnostic output.
skeleton_branch_length_hist_sample_*.png
aggregate_skeleton_branch_length_hist.png
.loop_paused
watchdog.log

